	IDS_HELP_TITLE, "Help"
	IDS_HELP_HEADING, "xucRun - Launch applications in another user context"
	IDS_HELP_USAGE, "Start applications:\n• {0} <application> [arguments...]\n  Automatic account and privilege selection.\n• {0} [user switch] <application> [arguments...]\n  /user[:<username>] keeps the current privilege mode.\n  /user-elevated[:<username>] requires elevation or aborts.\n• {0} /hidden [user switch] <application> [arguments...]\n  Hides only the immediate application.\n• {0} /hidden-monitor [user switch] <application> [arguments...]\n  Also reports a nonzero exit code.\n\nManage credentials:\n• {0} /addcred [<username>] - store credentials securely\n• {0} /deletecred [<username>] - delete credentials\n• {0} /showcred - show stored accounts\n\nManage approvals:\n• {0} /showapprovals - show stored approvals\n• {0} /resetapprovals[:<username>] - select approvals to reset\n\nManage backups:\n• {0} /backup - open the backup management window\n• {0} /backup-create [<description>] - create a backup\n• {0} /backup-list - list available backups\n• {0} /backup-restore - select a backup to restore\n• {0} /backup-restore:<backup-ID> - restore a backup directly\n• {0} /backup-delete-all - delete all backups\n\nStatus and diagnostics:\n• {0} /admin-status - show stored data for all users\n• {0} /clear-all - delete all xucRun data\n• {0} /audit - run security diagnostics\n• {0} /help, {0} --help, {0} /? - show this help\n• Aliases: --hidden, --hidden-monitor\n\n"
	IDS_HELP_EXAMPLES, "Examples:\n• Standard launch:\n  {0} notepad.exe\n• Another account with unchanged privileges:\n  {0} /user:Administrator notepad.exe\n• Guaranteed elevation:\n  {0} /user-elevated:Administrator notepad.exe\n• Hidden launch with exit-code monitoring:\n  {0} /hidden-monitor cmd.exe /c task.cmd\n• Store credentials:\n  {0} /addcred DOMAIN\\AdminUser\n  The password is requested on a protected private desktop.\n\n"
	IDS_HELP_NOTES, "Important notes:\n• Credentials are bound to the SID of the signed-in Windows user and stored by the LocalSystem broker.\n• Without a user switch, administrator accounts are preferred and launched elevated. One matching account is selected automatically; multiple accounts are offered for selection. Standard accounts are used only when no administrator account is available.\n• For the current administrator account, an existing elevated state is retained or Windows UAC is requested automatically.\n• /user keeps the privilege mode unchanged; without a user name, one stored account is selected automatically or multiple accounts are offered.\n• /user-elevated guarantees elevation; without a user name, only stored administrator accounts are offered.\n• /hidden and /hidden-monitor affect only the immediate application. Its dialogs and child processes remain visible. /hidden-monitor evaluates only the exit code and does not capture output.\n• /resetapprovals without a user name can also reset profile-wide approvals; a targeted user call leaves them unchanged.\n• Backups contain all broker data, are bound to this computer, and cannot be transferred to another computer.\n• /clear-all permanently deletes all xucRun data for all Windows profiles on this computer and stops the broker service.\n• /audit checks the running client, installed Core files, signatures, certificate, broker policy and ACLs, configuration, and an optional Tray installation without reading credentials.\n• A user switch without an application replaces the current console in the selected mode."
	IDS_HELP_INFO, "Runtime information:\n• {0} /info - show versions, signing certificate, broker status, account, configuration, and stored-data counts\n\n"
	IDS_INFO_TITLE, "Information"
	IDS_INFO_HEADING, "xucRun runtime information"
